  "notes": [
    "One D-Point per Rp 2.500, the same base rate as the JCB Precious, and the same D-Point currency, so the mileage ratios are the ones that card publishes.",
    "The card’s headline benefits are cashback, not points: 10% back on weekend spending, up to Rp 200.000 a month and only with five transactions of at least Rp 100.000 each, and 5% back on bill payments up to Rp 100.000 a month. Neither is written as a rule — a rule cannot match a day of the week, and a program earns in one unit, which here is points.",
    "The annual fee is Rp 600.000 and the bank waives it on conditions it does not publish in one place. Set what you are actually charged on the card terms.",
    "Transfer ratios are copied from the Danamon JCB Precious, since both cards spend the same D-Point balance. If Danamon prices conversions differently by card, this is wrong; nothing found suggests it does."
  ],
